{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "project": "Torpedo Room",
  "version": "0.1.23-beta",
  "prepared_at_utc": "2026-10-21T19:28:53+00:00",
  "changes": [
    "Keep native viewing tube selection accessible at depth; move depth gate to Feuer in all report modes, preserving native checkbox/selector relationship. Add active Prep border. Enlarge original Hidden/MP Feuer 1.5x and follow opener with scaled spacing/nearby-control avoidance and fallback. Retain TRC9 and Workshop item 3823181610."
  ],
  "validation": {
    "compile": "passed",
    "offline": "passed",
    "in_game": "not-run",
    "notes": [
      "Full supplied UBOAT/Unity/Harmony reference compilation passed. 269 targeted offline assertions passed: 85 stock/depth, 99 viewing fire/layout, 50 MP display, 35 UI affordance. New T5 deselect/reselect, mixed-selection correction, shallow recovery, border and scaled dock tests use actual classes with native/Unity/MP fixtures. Other suites not re-run. No live .23 rendering/firing/network execution. License/credits unchanged."
    ]
  },
  "known_issues": [
    "Live .23 Unity rendering/hit testing, exact fired indices, MP host/client and scale/resolution geometry need testing. Native half-full flooding graphic remains under investigation, not claimed fixed. Prior .22 logs record Tube V launch verified=True and whole-panel lockout; this patch addresses its depth overlay. Multi-tube Prep editing remains future work. No config migration or new release/tag/Workshop upload."
  ],
